# 💳 Core PHP Visa Gateway Integration — Razorpay

[![PHP](https://img.shields.io/badge/PHP-7.4%20%7C%208.x-777BB4?style=for-the-badge\&logo=php\&logoColor=white)](https://www.php.net/)
[![MySQL](https://img.shields.io/badge/MySQL-5.7%20%7C%208.0-4479A1?style=for-the-badge\&logo=mysql\&logoColor=white)](https://www.mysql.com/)
[![Razorpay](https://img.shields.io/badge/Payment-Razorpay%20Test%20Mode-0C2340?style=for-the-badge\&logo=razorpay\&logoColor=white)](https://razorpay.com/)
[![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-green.svg?style=for-the-badge)](LICENSE)

A simple end-to-end **Visa Application Payment Gateway** project built with **Core PHP, MySQL, MySQLi, cURL, JavaScript, and Razorpay**.

The project demonstrates how a PHP application can create a server-side payment order, launch a hosted payment checkout, receive the payment response, verify the Razorpay signature on the server, and update the transaction status in MySQL.

The project intentionally avoids Laravel, Symfony, Composer SDKs, and other full-stack frameworks so that the complete payment flow remains easy to understand.

> **Important:** This project is intended primarily for learning, development, and testing. Before using a payment system in production, additional controls such as webhooks, idempotency, HTTPS, secure secret management, detailed audit logging, access control, and reconciliation should be implemented.

